## First-round evidence — 2026-09-14

Frozen acceptance brief committed as 844888af before external research.
Documentary artifacts: docs/jetp-audits/0736/report.md and linked chronology,
comparator/rival/allocation matrices, sources.csv and acquisition-log.csv.

Exactly 20 external units used (7 queries, 12 web opens, 1 failed shell URL
retrieval); no second round. First documentary check passes with stated gaps:
South Africa events separated; India not automatically untreated. Senegal plan
publication unverified through failed original route; no usable country
allocation rule established. Direct Council URL reopens failed, but the parent
subsequently verified the cached original extraction independently. No source
bytes archived, no ledger changes, no estimation. Documentary exit criteria
passed scientific review; ticket stays open until PR acceptance.

## Independent review

All five documentary exit criteria are addressed as a bounded evidence audit;
this does not establish a usable causal design or complete historical population.
An independent scientific reviewer accepted the report and matrices. Fast gate:
1549 passed, ten skipped; adherence:330 passed, thirteen skipped. The report
records the missing-DVC environment failure and successful hydrated rerun.
Ticket remains open until the report PR is accepted.
